lazytv (1.1.2-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Keyboard hotkeys on the remote screen: arrows, Enter/Space (OK),
    Esc (BACK), Backspace (EXIT), P, M, H, I, +/- for volume,
    PageUp/PageDown for channels, digits 0-9 (main row and numpad),
    Tab switches between the main and numeric pages.
  * Hotkeys flash the matching on-screen button; auto-repeat is allowed
    only for arrows, volume and channel and is capped by the client
    command interval, so a held key cannot flood the TV. Ctrl/Alt/Meta
    combinations are not intercepted.
  * New "Hotkeys" toggle in settings, stored as hotkeysEnabled in
    ~/.config/lazytv/config.json (enabled by default).
  * Updated application icon: simpler shape, better legibility at
    small sizes.
  * Docs: keyboard hotkeys section in README and release notes 1.1.2.

 -- mindwork64 <vmurashov85@gmail.com>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:30:00 +0300
lazytv (1.1.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Read the HTTP response body by Content-Length instead of waiting for
    socket disconnect — commands no longer get lost on a slow TV.
  * Handle session expiry: on HTTP 401 the client emits sessionExpired,
    clears the saved session and returns to the pairing screen.
  * Parse ROAPError/ROAPErrorDetail so a rejected command reports why.
  * Block the pairing "request code" button for 60 s after a success
    (a repeated request invalidates the code shown on the TV).
  * Settings screen: show the version from the build instead of a
    hardcoded string.
  * Packaging: trailing newline in debian/{changelog,control,rules},
    add scripts/release-ppa.sh and release notes for 1.1.1.

 -- mindwork64 <vmurashov85@gmail.com>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:39:28 +0300
